  "summary": "A style combining Baroque elements with Edwardian elegance and restraint.",
  "description": "Characterized by grand proportions, classical details, and a more restrained ornamentation than Victorian styles. It emerged during King Edward VII's reign as a reaction against the excesses of Victorian architecture while maintaining formal dignity and imperial grandeur.",
  "culturalContext": "Edwardian Baroque (1901-1914) — the confidence style of Britain's imperial apex — fused Wren and Vanbrugh's English Baroque with Beaux-Arts planning for civic giants: Liverpool's Port of Liverpool Building, Belfast City Hall, London's Old Bailey. Wearing Portland stone, giant coupled columns, sculpted attics and domed towers, it projected municipal pride until WWI punctured the certainties; modernists would later mock its \"wedding cake\" massing even as conservationists fought for it.",
